@page
@model Portfolio.Pages.Projects.MlmLinkupModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "MLMLinkup";
}
<header class="page-header">
    <p class="page-kicker">
        <i class="bi bi-kanban" aria-hidden="true"></i> Independent software
    </p>
    <h1>
        @ViewData["Title"]
    </h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
        Two recorded iterations of a full stack learning project and direct-sales marketing service.
    </p>
    <p class="historical-context">
        Historical project description: plans, status, and technology references below reflect the recorded project period. No current status update has been supplied.
    </p>
</header>
<nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Related project pages">
    <a asp-page="/Projects/Index">All projects</a><a asp-page="/Git">Public repositories</a>
</nav>
<nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Project sections">
    <a href="#section-1">MLMLinkup Project 2016</a><a href="#section-2">MLMLinkup Project 2019</a>
</nav>
<section id="section-1" class="reading-layout">
    <article class="reading-main prose">
        <h2>
            MLMLinkup Project 2016
        </h2>
        <p>
            As a developer, it is important to function in all capacities within and without the application stack.
            My predominant skills have been developed primarily for the coding in the lower layers of most applications.
            Because of this I have gained a great deal of proficiency and experience in the lower layers of application
            development methods and architecture.
        </p>
        <p>
            Rounding out my skills was a paramount importance for me and is still a work in progress.
            A number of development firms are seeking those developers who have strong developmental skills in all layers of the
            application stack and lifecycle. MLMLinkup is my playground for learning front end development and building out my
            portfolio as a full stack developer.
        </p>
        @*
        <p>
        <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://MLMLinkup.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MLMLinkup.com >></a>
        </p>
        *@
    </article>
    <aside class="reading-aside content-panel" aria-label="Technology details">
        <h3>
            Technology
        </h3>
        <p>
            Some of the Technologies utilized in its development:
        </p>
        <ul class="tag-list">
            <li>
                Azure Hosted
            </li>
            <li>
                Bootstrap, jQuery
            </li>
            <li>
                C#.NET, MVC Razor, ASP.NET
            </li>
            <li>
                Entity Framework, Unit of Work, Repository Models
            </li>
            <li>
                Enabled <a href="https://letsencrypt.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Let's Encrypt</a> on Azure Web Applications
            </li>
            <li>
                PayPal Merchant API
            </li>
            <li>
                reCAPTCHA
            </li>
            <li>
                Sendgrid
            </li>
            <li>
                SQL Server
            </li>
            <li>
                Twilio
            </li>
            <li>
                Wordpress
            </li>
        </ul>
    </aside>
</section>
<section id="section-2" class="reading-layout">
    <article class="reading-main prose">
        <h2>
            MLMLinkup Project 2019
        </h2>
        <p>
            I was not fully satisfied with the MLMLinkup product and went back to the drawing board and is currently under development. With the assistance
            of Russell W. Carey I am making a whole new approach to the UX / UI design and streamlining a number of the technological services that were originally
            baked into the MLMLinkup service. In this iteration I am moving the majority of services and jobs out of the MLMLinkup code base and into their own
            web services under the owner company, A Game Empowerment.
        </p>
        <p>
            <a class="btn btn-site" asp-area="" asp-page="/Projects/AGameEmpowerment">Learn more &gt;&gt;</a>
        </p>
        <p>
            This service is a multi part service and is made of two compontents. The primary service is the MLMLinkup.com website. This is the primary marketing site for
            Direct Sales Associates and Network Marketers. The second part is vip.MLMLinkup.com. This wordpress site is designed to be a marketing funnel to help draw in
            direct sales members looking to advertise thier business, individuals looking to do research, and finally individuals looking to purchase products from a sales
            associate.
        </p>
        @*
        <p>
        <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://MLMLinkup.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MLMLinkup.com >></a>
        <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://vip.MLMLinkup.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vip.MLMLinkup.com >></a>
        </p>
        *@
    </article>
    <aside class="reading-aside content-panel" aria-label="Technology details">
        <h3>
